---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const canonicalUrl = 'https://handheldsettings.com/steam-deck-settings/cyberpunk-2077/';
const title = 'Best Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck settings: Verified 30 FPS baseline — Handheld Settings Lab';
const description = 'Tune Cyberpunk 2077 on Steam Deck with a Valve Verified default-first workflow, cautious 800p/30 FPS baseline, repeatable Night City tests, and 70GB SSD planning.';
const image = '/assets/games/cyberpunk-2077-header.jpg';

const sources = [
  {
    label: 'Steam: Cyberpunk 2077 store data, PC requirements, controller support, and official media',
    url: 'https://store.steampowered.com/app/1091500/Cyberpunk_2077/'
  },
  {
    label: 'Steam: current Steam Deck compatibility report for app 1091500',
    url: 'https://store.steampowered.com/saleaction/ajaxgetdeckappcompatibilityreport?nAppID=1091500'
  },
  {
    label: 'CD PROJEKT RED Support: Cyberpunk 2077 system requirements',
    url: 'https://support.cdprojektred.com/en/cyberpunk/pc/sp-technical/issue/1556/cyberpunk-2077-system-requirements'
  },
  {
    label: 'Valve: Steam Deck technical specifications',
    url: 'https://www.steamdeck.com/en/tech'
  }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What are the best Cyberpunk 2077 settings for Steam Deck?',
    answer: 'Test the game’s Steam Deck preset and Valve’s Verified default first. For a manual consistency profile, start at 1280×800, cap at 30 FPS, disable ray tracing, use FSR Quality or the closest current quality-oriented upscaler, and keep crowd density, screen-space reflections, volumetric fog, volumetric clouds, cascaded shadows, and ambient occlusion Low. This is a cautious editorial baseline, not a personally measured guarantee.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Is Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck Verified?',
    answer: 'Yes. Valve’s current compatibility endpoint resolves Cyberpunk 2077 as category 3, Verified. It reports functional default controls, matching controller glyphs, legible interface text, and a performant default configuration. Verified is a compatibility assessment, not a promise that every Night City scene holds one frame rate.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should I use 30 FPS or 40 FPS for Cyberpunk 2077 on Steam Deck?',
    answer: 'Use capped 30 FPS as the first consistency target. Dense traffic, crowds, combat, weather, and fast driving can stress the system differently. Try 40 only as an experiment after the 30 FPS profile passes the same demanding route, and return to 30 if frame pacing becomes uneven.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should ray tracing be enabled on Steam Deck?',
    answer: 'No for this baseline. Keep every ray-tracing option off while establishing performance. The handheld’s rendering budget is better spent on consistent frame pacing and readable image quality.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How much storage does Cyberpunk 2077 need on Steam Deck?',
    answer: 'Steam and CD PROJEKT RED currently list 70GB of available space and require an SSD in the PC requirements. Leave additional free space for patches, shader data, saves, Steam’s update process, and any installed expansion or optional content. Check the current Steam install dialog for the actual download on your account.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Were these Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck settings benchmarked?',
    answer: 'No. Handheld Settings Lab did not personally benchmark the current game build, SteamOS version, compatibility layer, battery runtime, or thermals. This page combines current official requirements and Valve compatibility information with a conservative, repeatable tuning method.'
  }
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'TechArticle',
    headline: 'Best Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck settings: Verified 30 FPS baseline',
    description,
    image: `https://handheldsettings.com${image}`,
    url: canonicalUrl,
    datePublished: '2026-08-07',
    dateModified: '2026-08-07',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Handheld Settings Lab' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Handheld Settings Lab', url: 'https://handheldsettings.com/' },
    about: ['Cyberpunk 2077', 'Steam Deck', 'game settings', 'frame rate', 'handheld PC']
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://handheldsettings.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Steam Deck settings', item: 'https://handheldsettings.com/steam-deck-settings/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Cyberpunk 2077 settings', item: canonicalUrl }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map(faq => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: faq.question,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer }
    }))
  }
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} image={image} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="wrap article">
    <span class="eyebrow">Steam Deck settings · Baseline published August 2026</span>
    <h1>Best Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck settings: start with a stable 30 FPS profile</h1>
    <p class="lede muted">Cyberpunk 2077 is Steam Deck Verified and includes a handheld-friendly starting point, but Night City can move quickly from an interior to dense crowds, traffic, rain, combat, and fast driving. Test the supported default first, then use this cautious 800p/30 profile to diagnose demanding routes. This is official-source-informed guidance—not a personally tested benchmark.</p>

    <figure class="game-hero">
      <img src={image} alt="Official Cyberpunk 2077 Steam header artwork showing V against the Night City skyline" width="460" height="215" />
      <figcaption class="media-credit">Official Cyberpunk 2077 Steam store header image, saved locally from <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1091500/Cyberpunk_2077/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">CD PROJEKT RED's Steam store page</a>. Artwork and trademarks belong to their owners; use does not imply endorsement.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="settings-panel">
      <section class="card"><h3>Consistency target</h3><div class="stat">800p / 30</div><p class="muted">Cautious starting baseline</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Starting point</h3><p><strong>Steam Deck preset</strong></p><p class="muted">Test the supported default first</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Compatibility</h3><p><strong>Deck Verified</strong></p><p class="muted">Valve report checked August 7, 2026</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Storage floor</h3><div class="stat">70GB</div><p class="muted">Official requirement; SSD required</p></section>
    </div>

    <div class="callout"><strong>Use a real Night City test loop:</strong> drive through a crowded district, leave the vehicle, turn the camera across traffic and pedestrians, then enter one combat encounter. Repeat the same route twice after each change. An apartment or inventory screen cannot prove the profile is stable.</div>

    <h2>Recommended Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck baseline</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Start here</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Compatibility tool</td><td>Valve default</td><td>The current compatibility report is Verified. Do not force an old Proton build before testing the supported path.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Quick preset</td><td>Steam Deck, then customize</td><td>Establishes the game’s handheld-oriented default before you make controlled changes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resolution</td><td>1280×800</td><td>Uses the Deck display’s 16:10 canvas and preserves interface space.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Frame-rate cap</td><td>30 FPS</td><td>Prioritizes consistency across crowds, traffic, combat, and streaming-heavy traversal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Upscaling</td><td>FSR Quality first</td><td>Preserves more image detail for the initial comparison. Try Balanced only if the same route remains below target.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Texture quality</td><td>Medium</td><td>Retains surface clarity; reduce only if repeated asset-streaming or memory symptoms point here.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Field of view</td><td>Default</td><td>A wider view can increase the scene visible at once. Tune for comfort after the performance baseline.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Crowd density</td><td>Low</td><td>Reduces population pressure in busy districts and creates headroom while driving.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Screen-space reflections</td><td>Low</td><td>Night City contains many wet, glossy, and reflective surfaces; this is a useful early cost reduction.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ambient occlusion</td><td>Low</td><td>Keeps the diagnostic profile conservative in dense scenes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Volumetric fog / clouds</td><td>Low</td><td>Reduces atmospheric rendering load during weather and broad city views.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cascaded shadow range / resolution</td><td>Low</td><td>Lowers the cost of dynamic shadows across outdoor streets.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Local shadow quality</td><td>Medium</td><td>Preserves some close-range definition while the broader shadow settings stay Low.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Level of detail</td><td>Medium</td><td>Maintains useful city geometry detail; move to Low if fast driving remains the repeatable failure.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Motion blur / film grain / chromatic aberration</td><td>Off for testing</td><td>Makes image clarity and pacing easier to compare. Re-enable only by preference.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ray tracing</td><td>Off</td><td>Keeps the handheld baseline focused on rasterized performance.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Steam Deck TDP limit</td><td>Off for first test</td><td>Do not constrain device power before the graphics profile passes the repeated route.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">Setting names and available upscalers can change with game updates. Use the closest current option and save screenshots before editing. Official desktop-PC requirements provide useful storage and feature context; they do not guarantee a Steam Deck frame rate.</p>

    <h2>Compare two profiles without changing everything</h2>
    <div class="grid cols2">
      <section class="card">
        <span class="chip">Profile A · supported baseline</span>
        <h3>Steam Deck preset / 30 FPS</h3>
        <p>Use Valve’s default compatibility tool and the game’s Steam Deck preset at 800p with a 30 FPS cap. Run the full driving, crowd, and combat loop twice before customizing it.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card">
        <span class="chip">Profile B · consistency custom</span>
        <h3>800p / 30 FPS / selective Low</h3>
        <p>Keep textures and level of detail Medium, use FSR Quality, and lower crowds, reflections, ambient occlusion, volumetrics, and cascaded shadows. Use Balanced upscaling only as the next isolated test.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <h2>A repeatable tuning order</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Update, then restart.</strong> Finish the stable game, SteamOS, and shader downloads before diagnosing a recurring problem.</li>
      <li><strong>Test the Verified default.</strong> Valve currently reports functional default controls, matching glyphs, legible text, and a performant default configuration. Record how it behaves before replacing it.</li>
      <li><strong>Apply one frame target.</strong> Begin at capped 30 FPS with no Steam Deck TDP limit.</li>
      <li><strong>Repeat the same route twice.</strong> Include driving, crowds, rapid camera movement, and combat. A second pass helps separate one-time asset or shader work from sustained pressure.</li>
      <li><strong>Lower city-scene costs first.</strong> Keep crowds, reflections, volumetrics, ambient occlusion, and cascaded shadows Low before sacrificing texture clarity.</li>
      <li><strong>Change upscaling alone.</strong> Compare FSR Quality and Balanced on the same route without changing the cap or graphics table.</li>
      <li><strong>Tune battery last.</strong> Lower the Deck TDP limit in small steps only after the profile passes. Stop when pacing worsens, then return to the previous step.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Fix common Cyberpunk 2077 Steam Deck problems</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Check first</th><th>Next step</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Driving through crowds misses the cap</td><td>Confirm Low crowd density, reflections, fog, clouds, and cascaded shadows</td><td>Try Balanced upscaling, then Low level of detail if fast travel remains the repeatable failure</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Brief hitch on a new route</td><td>Pause downloads and run the identical route a second time</td><td>Check free SSD space and restore Valve’s default compatibility tool before broad graphics cuts</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Image is too soft</td><td>Return to FSR Quality at 800p and disable film grain and chromatic aberration for comparison</td><td>Keep the 30 FPS cap and Medium textures instead of raising several expensive scene settings</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Text or HUD is hard to read</td><td>Use native 800p output and review the current accessibility and interface text-size controls</td><td>Reduce extra scaling or sharpening layers before lowering resolution again</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Battery drains faster than expected</td><td>Confirm the 30 FPS cap, brightness, wireless use, and total system draw</td><td>Lower TDP gradually only after the route is stable; use your observed draw in the battery estimator</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Controls or button prompts changed</td><td>Restore the official/default Steam Input layout</td><td>Remove per-game remaps one at a time before changing Proton</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Crashes began after an update</td><td>Restart, verify files, restore the Steam Deck preset, and turn ray tracing off</td><td>Remove unofficial launch options or configuration edits and check CD PROJEKT RED Support for a current issue</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Storage, battery, and offline planning</h2>
    <p>Steam and CD PROJEKT RED currently list <strong>70GB of available space</strong>, DirectX 12, and an SSD requirement. Steam also lists full controller support, Steam Cloud, adjustable text size, subtitle options, and several accessibility features. Keep additional room for patches, shader data, saves, Steam’s update process, and installed optional content. Check the current install dialog, then model the rest of your library in the <a href="/calculators/storage-planner/">storage planner</a>.</p>
    <p>This page does not invent a battery runtime. Steam Deck LCD and OLED capacities differ, while frame cap, brightness, crowds, combat, wireless activity, and device power change consumption. Read total system draw on your repeated route and enter it in the <a href="/calculators/battery-estimator/">battery estimator</a>. Compare the site’s labeled planning ranges in the <a href="/guides/steam-deck-battery-life-by-game/">battery-by-game guide</a>.</p>
    <p>Steam lists Cyberpunk 2077 as single-player, but launcher state, updates, cloud saves, and account checks can still affect a trip. Before travel, complete the <a href="/guides/handheld-pc-offline-mode-flight-checklist/">offline-mode flight checklist</a> and prove a disconnected launch from the save you intend to use.</p>

    <h2>Optional gear after the settings are stable</h2>
    <p class="affiliate-note">Disclosure: these are broad Amazon searches marked sponsored/nofollow, not hands-on endorsements. Compare exact specifications, seller traceability, device fit, warranty, and return terms. No price, compatibility, performance, or battery claim is made; a real Associates tag is appended only when configured.</p>
    <div class="grid cols3">
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=steam+deck+microSD+card+a2+uhs+i" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="microsd-cards">
        <span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>A2 UHS-I microSD cards</h3><p class="muted">Compare genuine capacity, seller traceability, warranty, and room beyond the current 70GB base-game requirement.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=steam+deck+45w+usb+c+pd+power+bank" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="power-banks">
        <span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>45W USB-C PD power banks</h3><p class="muted">Check dedicated-port output, printed watt-hours, cable rating, weight, and current airline rules instead of relying on mAh alone.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=steam+deck+oled+carrying+case+charger+storage" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="cases">
        <span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>Steam Deck travel cases</h3><p class="muted">Compare exact LCD/OLED fit, stick pressure, charger separation, airflow after play, and bag dimensions.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p>Use the <a href="/guides/best-microsd-cards-for-handheld-gaming/">microSD comparison method</a>, check the <a href="/guides/usb-c-power-bank-wattage-handheld-gaming/">power-bank and airline guide</a>, or browse the <a href="/gear/">spec-based gear library</a>.</p>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="grid cols2">
      {faqs.map(faq => (
        <section class="card">
          <h3>{faq.question}</h3>
          <p>{faq.answer}</p>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2>Sources and methodology</h2>
    <p>Sources were checked on August 7, 2026. Steam’s public store data supplies the 70GB SSD requirement, DirectX 12 requirement, full controller support, accessibility and cloud-save labels, developer/publisher identity, and official image. Valve’s live compatibility endpoint currently resolves Cyberpunk 2077 as Deck Verified and reports functional default controls, matching glyphs, legible interface text, and a performant default configuration. CD PROJEKT RED supplies the official system-requirements and support route, while Valve supplies Steam Deck hardware context. The profiles above are conservative editorial testing sequences informed by those official constraints and common graphics-cost relationships. Handheld Settings Lab did not personally benchmark the current game, SteamOS, compatibility layer, battery, or thermals. Google autocomplete evidence saved in the July 2026 audit includes “best Steam Deck settings for Cyberpunk 2077”; that is query-language evidence, not search volume.</p>
    <ul>
      {sources.map(source => <li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">{source.label}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p>For more games, return to the <a href="/steam-deck-settings/">Steam Deck settings hub</a>. Compare the <a href="/rog-ally-settings/cyberpunk-2077/">ROG Ally Cyberpunk 2077 baseline</a> or <a href="/legion-go-settings/cyberpunk-2077/">Legion Go Cyberpunk 2077 baseline</a>, use the <a href="/calculators/">battery, storage, and accessory calculators</a>, or browse the <a href="/gear/">gear library</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
